From the 021 console run. Most lost draws came from shaders whose texture handle is one word of a
wider load, which the draw-time handle programs did not cover, so the search they fell back to threw
and the pipeline was lost. Handle programs now read words of 3- and 4-word loads and of assembled
vectors, drop the words of a path that failed, and a handle that still cannot be computed samples
handle 0 instead of losing the pipeline. The 2D gather also takes depth compare. The texture decoder
no longer ends the session when a large block is refused: it asks for a collection, retries for 3 s
and then leaves that texture blank.

